  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="updated">Last updated: October 2026</div>

  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Piaggio Group Americas, Inc. ("PGA," "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and protects information in connection with the PGA Dealer Portal at mypiaggio.com (the "Portal"). The Portal is a business tool provided to authorized PGA dealers and staff. By using the Portal, you agree to the practices described here.</p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>The Portal is operated by Piaggio Group Americas, Inc. For questions about this policy or your information, contact us at <a class="inline" href="mailto:support@us.piaggio.com">support@us.piaggio.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information:</strong> your name, business email, phone number, job position, dealership affiliation, and the access level assigned to you.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage information:</strong> sign-in activity, the dates and times you access the Portal, and the features you use, which we use to operate and improve the service.</li>
    <li><strong>Business data:</strong> dealership inventory, sales, order, allocation, and related records made available to you through the Portal in your role.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> standard information your browser provides, such as device and browser type, needed to deliver the Portal securely.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide, secure, and maintain the Portal and your account.</li>
    <li>To show you the inventory, orders, allocations, promotions, and reporting relevant to your dealership and role.</li>
    <li>To communicate with you about your account, support requests, and service updates.</li>
    <li>To understand how the Portal is used so we can improve it.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. How we share information</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share information only as needed to run the Portal:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Within PGA:</strong> with authorized PGA staff who need it to manage dealer relationships and the Portal.</li>
    <li><strong>Service providers:</strong> trusted vendors who host and support the Portal on our behalf, under confidentiality obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal reasons:</strong> when required by law, regulation, or valid legal process, or to protect the rights and safety of PGA, our dealers, and others.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Confidentiality of dealer data</h2>
  <p>Information in the Portal, including allocations, pricing, availability, and inventory, is confidential and provided for authorized PGA dealers and staff only. You agree not to distribute or disclose it outside your dealership or beyond your authorized use.</p>

  <h2>6. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>The Portal uses only the cookies and local storage necessary to keep you signed in and to make the Portal work. We do not use the Portal to serve advertising.</p>

  <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
  <p>We keep account and usage information for as long as your account is active and as needed to provide the Portal, meet legal and recordkeeping requirements, and resolve disputes. Business data is retained in line with PGA's records practices.</p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>We use administrative, technical, and organizational measures to protect information, including access controls that limit each user to the data appropriate for their role. No system is perfectly secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security, but we work to protect your information and keep access limited to authorized users.</p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you are located, you may have the right to access, correct, update, or request deletion of your personal information, and to ask questions about how it is handled. To make a request, contact <a class="inline" href="mailto:support@us.piaggio.com">support@us.piaggio.com</a>. We will respond consistent with applicable law.</p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>The Portal is a business tool and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 16.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Last updated" date above, and significant changes may be communicated through the Portal.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
  <p>Questions about this Privacy Policy or your information? Email <a class="inline" href="mailto:support@us.piaggio.com">support@us.piaggio.com</a>.</p>

